    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614">

                <pb facs="0713" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg617"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tripp to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Apia, Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to submit herewith letters
                    received from Malietoa Tanumafili and also from Mataafa, together with our
                    replies.</p>
                <p>We have arranged to receive Malietoa Tanumafili this afternoon and Mataafa
                    to-morrow morning on board the <hi rendition="#italic">Badger</hi>, together
                    with their head chiefs and talking men. We shall hear what each party has to
                    say, advise them fully of our powers, and inform them that they must disband,
                    return to their homes, and await the further action of the commission.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>All is now quiet and the status quo is expected to be maintained until the
                    definite action of the commission.</p>
                <p>I am getting off this dispatch hurriedly just as the mail is closing, and beg,
                    etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bartlett Tripp.</hi></signed></closer>








